WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:02.660
- [Interviewer] I apologize for

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:06.000
the absurd philosophical question,

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.063
but if an alien species
were to visit earth,

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.800
do you think we would be able
to find a common language,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.530
or protocol of communication with them?

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:20.200
- [Noam] There are arguments
to the effect that we could,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.330
in fact, one of them was Marv Minsky's.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.680
Back about 20 or 30 years ago,

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.400
he performed a sort of brief experiment

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.420
with a student of his, Dan Barlborough.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.420
They essentially ran the simplest
possible Turing machines,

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.990
just free, to see what would happen.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.980
And most of them crashed.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.690
Either got into an infinite loop,

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:50.230
or were flossed out.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.420
The few that persisted,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.890
essentially gave
something like arithmetic,

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:01.210
and his conclusion from that was that

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:07.390
if some alien species developed
a higher intelligence,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.860
they would at least have arithmetic,

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:10.810
they would at least have

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:15.350
what the simplest computer would do.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.460
And in fact, he didn't
know that at the time,

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.170
but the core principals
of natural language

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:27.130
are based on operations which yield

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.900
something like arithmetic,
in the limiting case,

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.780
and the minimal case.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.360
So it's conceivable

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.690
that a mode of communication
could be established

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:42.110
based on the core properties
of human language,

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:43.880
and the core properties of arithmetic,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.033
which maybe are universally shared.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.443
So it's conceivable.

